# Line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Context: this checkout runs on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so the
# repository stores LF while the working tree is CRLF.  That is a working
# arrangement -- do NOT force `eol=lf` tree-wide here.  Doing so would make
# every CRLF file in the working tree show up as modified in one shot and
# bury real changes under tens of thousands of whitespace-only diffs.
#
# What this file actually pins is the part that genuinely matters:
#   * text/binary classification, so Git never tries to "normalise" a blob
#     that would be corrupted by it (SQLite in particular);
#   * the few extensions whose line endings are load-bearing at runtime.

# ── Text sources ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `text` (no eol) = store LF in the repository, use the platform-native form
# in the working tree.  Matches the existing arrangement.
*.py    text
*.pyi   text
*.ts    text
*.tsx   text
*.js    text
*.jsx   text
*.mjs   text
*.cjs   text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.css   text
*.scss  text
*.html  text
*.qss   text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.toml  text
*.ini   text
*.cfg   text
*.txt   text
*.spec  text

# SVG is XML, not a binary blob -- keep it normalised and diffable.
*.svg   text

# ── Extensions where the line ending is load-bearing ────────────────────────
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 and cmd.exe both require CRLF; an LF-only .ps1 fails
# to parse on the platform this project targets.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF.  CI runs on ubuntu-latest, where a CRLF shebang
# line makes the kernel look for `/bin/bash\r` and the script dies instantly.
# (The project ships no .sh of its own today; this guards future additions and
# any vendored scripts.)
*.sh    text eol=lf

# ── Binary -- never convert, never diff ─────────────────────────────────────
# A line-ending rewrite inside any of these produces a corrupt file, and for
# SQLite that means an unopenable database rather than a cosmetic diff.
*.db       binary
*.db-wal   binary
*.db-shm   binary
*.sqlite   binary
*.sqlite3  binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.webp     binary
*.avif     binary
*.ico      binary
*.bmp      binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.pyd      binary
*.so       binary
*.dylib    binary
*.dll      binary
*.exe      binary
*.bundle   binary
*.zip      binary
*.mp4      binary
*.webm     binary
*.pdf      binary
